{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965764-new-totem-florida-man","id":965764,"title":"New Totem: Florida Man","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-08T11:26:37-07:00","id":965764,"title":"New Totem: Florida Man","content":"For your consideration (and criticism):<br /> <br /> Florida Man<br /> Totem of Cunning<br /> Cost: 3<br /> <br /> Rumored to have once been the humble City Father of Daytona Beach, the spiritual influence of Florida Man has expanded and grown significantly in recent years, especially thanks to dozens of news stories going viral on the internet that have spread an image like wildfire through the minds of Americans and beyond. The Glass Walkers theorize Florida Man represents the decay of human society and culture, and might later evolve into a Wyrm Totem as the Apocalypse grows nearer. The BoneGnawers celebrate Florida Man's emergence as a sign the Wyld might still flourish amidst the ever-thickening webs of the Weaver.<br /> <br /> Individual Traits: Florida Man's followers are Garou of the people (or the people of Florida, at least). They gain +1 die on any social dealings involving Floridians with Resources ratings of 2 or less. These same people are also more likely to have a positive first impression of the Garou (until given a reason to feel otherwise) or aid them in safe and simple ways. Any tribe other than BoneGnawers suffer a penalty of 1 Temporary Honor for aligning themselves with Florida Man.<br /> <br /> Pack Traits: Florida Man's packs enjoy two extra dice to Subterfuge rolls. Additionally, one member of the pack at any time can channel Florida Man's unique ability to make the insane seem mundane. The Garou can spin an explanation or frame the truth in such a manner that despite everyone present recognizing it as freakish or obscene, no one seems to care or give it a second thought. Blaming that faceless corpse on a hobo on bath salts, explaining the pack's nudity and assault weapons on an angry wife kicking them out of the trailer, or presenting a taco in lieu of proper identification... all will be accepted as &quot;normal&quot; without question or a follow-up investigation by the news or authorities (though in the case of particularly heinous crimes they might still attempt to throw the Garou in the drunk tank for the night.) The situation presented in the lie must ALWAYS be shameful, eccentric, or vulgar. Florida Man's realm of influence does not extend into simple or practical explanations, nor does it reach beyond the state's borders. Mechanically, this ability works identically to the gift Beautiful Lie (W20, 427), however anytime the pack must write themselves into the story to avoid unwanted attention or minimize the reaction of Law Enforcement, each pack member loses 2 Temporary Renown, chosen by the Storyteller, based on the nature and details of the tale they spin. <br /> <br /> Ban: Florida Man feels the pain of the poor and mentally afflicted and commands his packs to do the same. Followers of Florida Man can never enjoy a lifestyle above Resources 2 and must devoted at least a portion of their free time every week to aiding the poor or mentally ill in Florida, and often sends his followers portents of those in need of their help. Failing in this Ban or ignoring a portent (even if the Garou have something they consider &quot;more important&quot; to do) draws Florida Man's ire. He doesn't withdraw his boons, but instead inflicts a Derangement (Storyteller's choice, though usually one thematic to the reason for dereliction) on his followers until they resume their duties and atone twiceover for their arrogance.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T00:28:14-07:00","id":967804,"title":"","content":"This is very appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}